@startuml claim-survives-handoff
title A Claim Survives CP3A's Handoff Mid-Flight

skinparam defaultFontName Monospaced
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 1.5
skinparam sequenceParticipantBorderColor #888888
skinparam sequenceLifeLineBorderColor #AAAAAA
skinparam noteBorderColor #AAAAAA
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FAFAFA
skinparam sequenceGroupBorderColor #CCCCCC
skinparam sequenceGroupBodyBackgroundColor #FAFAFA

participant "Alert Evaluator" as AE #DBEAFE
participant "Redis" as R #FEF9C3
participant "Position Consumer" as PC #D1FAE5

AE -> R : CLAIM (Lua)\nKEYS = [alert-state:X, recent-loss:X]\nexpected dark_since_ms, candidate_id

note right of R
  Script checks alert-state:X first, finds a
  dark_since_ms match, composite_issued='0',
  no existing claim -> SUCCESS.
  composite_claim_candidate_id set on
  alert-state:X, in the SAME script call.
end note
R --> AE : claimed = true

PC -> R : entity resumes -- CP3A atomic handoff\n(unrelated trigger: whenever the entity resumes,\nnot in response to the claim above)

note right of R
  One Lua script transfers ALL current
  alert-state:X fields -- including
  composite_claim_candidate_id and
  composite_issued -- into recent-loss:X,
  then deletes alert-state:X. The claim set
  above is carried forward unconditionally;
  this script does not interpret it (see
  atomic-signal-loss-handoff).
end note

AE -> R : FINALIZE (Lua)\nSAME KEYS = [alert-state:X, recent-loss:X]\nsame expected dark_since_ms, same candidate_id

note right of R
  One script call: alert-state:X no longer
  has a dark_since_ms match (key is gone) --
  the SAME call falls through and checks
  recent-loss:X, finds the match, confirms
  the claim, sets composite_issued='1'.
  Not two round-trips -- one atomic script
  inspecting both keys.
end note
R --> AE : finalized = true

note over AE, PC
  Neither CLAIM nor FINALIZE needed to know,
  or be told, which representation held the
  episode at the moment each ran.
end note

@enduml
